var e=[{slug:`make-your-flowers-last`,title:`A little care, a little longer.`,category:`FLOWER CARE`,image:`/images/bouquet-2.jpg`,intro:`Simple rituals to keep your flowers happy, day after day.`,body:[`Start with a clean vase and fresh, room-temperature water. Remove any leaves that will sit below the waterline.`,`Trim the stems at an angle with clean, sharp scissors, then place them in water straight away. Use the flower food supplied with your arrangement according to its instructions.`,`Keep your flowers away from direct sunlight, heating vents, and ripening fruit. Refresh the water every two days and give the stems another small trim.`,`Remove faded flowers as you go. Every stem has its own rhythm, and a little attention makes the whole arrangement last longer.`]},{slug:`the-beauty-of-seasonal-flowers`,title:`Let the season choose.`,category:`FROM THE STUDIO`,image:`/images/bouquet-3.jpg`,intro:`Why our favorite arrangements begin with what’s growing now.`,body:[`Seasonal flowers bring a sense of place and time to an arrangement. They remind us to notice what is happening just outside our door.`,`In spring, we love the movement of tulips and ranunculus. Summer brings abundant garden roses and dahlias, while autumn invites richer colors and textural foliage.`,`A designer’s choice bouquet is an invitation to work with the most beautiful stems available that week. Your flowers may look a little different each time—that is part of their charm.`]}];export{e as t};